From: SlicerWeb <slicerweb@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] BUG: Reset the coincident topology offset uniforms of the low memory mapper

The low memory polydata mapper (the one OpenGL ES builds use for every model) applies
the coincident topology offset in the fragment shader, through the cOffset and cFactor
uniforms of vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology. The mod only uploaded them when the offset it
computed for the primitive at hand was not zero. Shader programs are shared, by source,
between every primitive type and every mapper, so a triangle draw with a zero polygon
offset ran with whatever the point or line draw before it had left in the program: the
default line offset of -4 units, or the point offset of -8. Every surface was therefore
drawn 4 depth units closer to the camera than it is; the mod's shader term is compiled in
even for surfaces, because the substitution is decided before the primitive type is set.

Markups control points, drawn by the regular mapper with the intended -1 unit, sank into
a model's surface wherever 4 units outweigh their radius: zooming in on a point placed on
a vessel wall made it disappear. The desktop mapper has the same "only when not zero"
rule, but never compiles the term into a zero-offset shader, so it cannot leak.

Upload the uniforms whenever the program has them, also when they are zero. And take the
point and line offsets for a surface shown as points or as wireframe, as the regular
mapper does. This is the vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology part of VTK commit e3c5c6f8
(2026-08-24, "Fix coincident topology offsets for the low memory mapper"), which also
re-enabled TestCoincident for the WebAssembly CI; the wireframe edge shading change of
that commit is not needed here.
---diff --git a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology.cxx b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology.cxx
index 0131b8f477..38cfd6f24c 100644
--- a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology.cxx
@@ -82,8 +82,10 @@ bool vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology::SetShaderParameters(vtkOpenGLRenderer* render
   float factor = 0.0;
   float offset = 0.0;
   this->GetCoincidentParameters(renderer, vtkMapper::SafeDownCast(mapper), actor, factor, offset);
-  if ((factor != 0.0 || offset != 0.0) && program->IsUniformUsed("cOffset") &&
-    program->IsUniformUsed("cFactor"))
+  // Set the uniforms whenever the program has them, also to zero: the program is shared by every
+  // primitive type and mapper whose shader source is the same, and a triangle draw that skipped
+  // them would keep the offset of the point or line draw before it.
+  if (program->IsUniformUsed("cOffset") && program->IsUniformUsed("cFactor"))
   {
     program->SetUniformf("cOffset", offset);
     program->SetUniformf("cFactor", factor);
@@ -116,11 +118,12 @@ void vtkGLSLModCoincidentTopology::GetCoincidentParameters(
   {
     double f = 0.0;
     double u = 0.0;
-    if (this->PrimitiveType == GL_POINTS)
+    if (this->PrimitiveType == GL_POINTS || ppty->GetRepresentation() == VTK_POINTS)
     {
       mapper->GetCoincidentTopologyPointOffsetParameter(u);
     }
-    else if (this->PrimitiveType == GL_LINES || this->PrimitiveType == GL_LINE_STRIP)
+    else if (this->PrimitiveType == GL_LINES || this->PrimitiveType == GL_LINE_STRIP ||
+      ppty->GetRepresentation() == VTK_WIREFRAME)
     {
       mapper->GetCoincidentTopologyLineOffsetParameters(f, u);
     }
